Tell the truth in five degraded states

The launcher is HOME on a unit whose vendor service, MCU, car kit and
storage can all be missing, blind or full. Five screens answered such a
state with a definite claim instead of an honest absence. Provoked one
at a time on emulator instance 2.

BLUETOOTH_CONNECT revoked at runtime: the profile probe and the
connection-state broadcasts both go silent, so the chip read "Bluetooth
on, nothing connected" - a phone mid-call would have shown as idle.
The count is now nullable and unreadable says so.

Ignition tile and the Power & sleep readout: CarEvents.accOn fails open
to true so a silent unit stays usable, and the tile printed that default
as "ACC on, vendor ACC broadcast" on a bench unit that has never heard
the car. A latched accSeen, the same shape as illuminationSeen, lets the
tile read as an em dash like every neighbour.

Notification access withdrawn while the shelf is open: the listener
detaches and the list empties, and the screen then said "0 showing,
Nothing new" - a claim about the phone. The access query is now keyed on
the binding, so it re-runs on the disconnect and the screen shows the
"access is off" copy it already had.

A btsuite page that is not installed, and a full or read-only /sdcard
under the backup and SysVar-export writers: all three calls already
return their failure, and all three screens dropped it, leaving a button
that silently does nothing. Each now says what did not happen.

Guards: DegradedReadingTest pins both absent-reading mappings, and a
fourth UiSourceAuditTest rule fails any ui/ file that drops one of those
fallible answers again.

Left: at font_scale 1.3 with density 280 the Vehicle dashboard clips its
tile captions and the bottom row falls off the panel. The fix is a
rework of the weighted grid, not a degraded-state change.

